// Regla Sigma: proc_creation_win_powershell_kerberos_kerberos_ticket_request_via_cli.yml
// ID Sigma: caa9a802-8bd8-4b9e-a5cd-4d6221670219
// Título: Suspicious Kerberos Ticket Request via CLI
// Descripción: Detects suspicious Kerberos ticket requests via command line using System.IdentityModel.Tokens.KerberosRequestorSecurityToken class.
Threat actors may use command line interfaces to request Kerberos tickets for service accounts in order to
perform offline password cracking attacks commonly known as Kerberoasting or other Kerberos ticket abuse
techniques like silver ticket attacks. Encoded commands will not surface the class name, so the ps_script
rule covers that instead.

// Fecha de creación: 2025-11-18
// Fecha de modificación: 2026-09-14
// Aplica a: Producto: windows | Categoría: process_creation
// Producto: windows
// Categoría: process_creation
// Servicio: 
// Nivel: high
// Pipeline: microsoft_xdr
// Ruta original: C:\SigmaLab\sigma\rules\windows\process_creation\proc_creation_win_powershell_kerberos_kerberos_ticket_request_via_cli.yml
// Requiere validación en el entorno de destino.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe") or (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName in~ ("powershell.exe", "pwsh.dll"))) and ProcessCommandLine contains "System.IdentityModel.Tokens.KerberosRequestorSecurityToken"
